about=bread('About this release')+intro('FIELD EDITION / 001','Built to help you go prepared.','A working first version—not a finished global marketplace.')+'''<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap narrow prose"><section><h2>What works today.</h2><p>Three starter destinations, three species references, six original preparation articles, personalized gear-status tracking, per-angler quantities, local browser saving, shareable snapshots, printable checklists, text exports, independent operator links, an inquiry builder and campaign-link tools.</p></section><section><h2>What is not connected.</h2><p>There is no live booking inventory, native checkout, escrow, cloud account, automated email delivery, central analytics collector or scheduled editorial update service in this release. Forms only send when the site owner enables and verifies hosted collection. Retailer links are searches, not vetted individual products.</p></section><section><h2>How information is presented.</h2><p>Destination and species pages link their reference sources. The preparation guides contain editorial suggestions, not field-tested endorsements. No operator is portrayed as a partner unless an agreement is actually established. Decorative map art is illustrative, not a navigational resource.</p></section><section><h2>Your saved plans.</h2><p>Plans are stored on this browser. Shared links contain a snapshot of trip inputs and gear statuses, not an email or account profile. Anyone with that link can read its contents. Editing one copy does not change other people’s copies. Clearing browser storage removes the local plan.</p></section><section><h2>Shopping and monetization.</h2><p>Amazon shopping links are untagged until the owner supplies an Associates tag. Where tagged links are enabled, qualifying purchases may earn a commission for Atlas. Product choice, price, stock and compatibility should be checked on the retailer’s page.</p></section><section><h2>A global product, starting with real depth.</h2><p>The structure supports more locations, species and guide content without rebuilding the planner. Expansion should add reliable guidance, useful shopping requirements and responsive operators, not pretend that a database entry is a complete fishing guide.</p></section></div></section>'''
